      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "GLM-5.3 NVFP4 , a quantized mixture-of-experts model with 753 billion parameters and 40 billion activated per token, requires about 464 GB of GPU memory, exceeding the 252 GB HBM3e on a single GB300 GPU.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:44.854Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Two NVIDIA DGX Stations connected over ConnectX-8 RDMA serve the model through one OpenAI-compatible endpoint using tensor parallelism (TP=2), with each GPU holding and computing roughly half the weights.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:44.854Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "vLLM launches a distributed service across both Stations, enabling multi-token prediction, FP8 KV-cache storage, and prefix caching to maximize throughput under concurrent load.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:44.854Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Two NVIDIA DGX Stations connected over ConnectX-8 RDMA serve one model through a single endpoint, with tensor parallelism splitting the model weights and computation across both GPUs.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:44.854Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Before starting, connect the two Stations with the Connect Two DGX Stations playbook .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:44.854Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This post shows how to serve GLM-5.3 locally across two NVIDIA DGX Stations with vLLM, send a request, and measure behavior under concurrent load.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:44.854Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Two GB300 DGX Stations running Linux, connected and validated with the Connect Two DGX Stations playbook , including its GPU-memory RDMA test on both rails.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:44.854Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This step turns two machines into one service: the same launch script runs on both Stations, reads ~/glm53.env , and starts one vLLM rank on each.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:44.854Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In nvidia-smi , A shows the VLLM::Worker_TP0 process and B shows VLLM::Worker_TP1 , one rank per GPU.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T17:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:44.854Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "You now have a 753-billion-parameter model running behind one local API on two NVIDIA DGX Stations, with every weight in GPU memory.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/when-one-gpu-isnt-enough-serving-glm-5-3-across-two-nvidia-dgx-stations-with-vllm/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
